// Source: "Wacatac malware detection and remediation" session (past chat)
// Purpose: full network activity for both malware families across the
// entire compromise window, one combined query.
// Result: confirmed the 147 vaelix.exe events (DC hits resolved to
// hqdc01/02/03.op.omniapartners.com). Zero Ditto.exe rows — despite Startup
// persistence, Ditto made no outbound network connections in this window
// (12:54 PM Jul 20 - 3:15 PM Jul 21). Clipboard capture tools typically
// don't need network activity to function, consistent with Ditto's role
// as a local capture tool rather than a network-beaconing implant.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where Timestamp between (datetime(2026-07-20T12:54:00) .. datetime(2026-07-21T15:15:00))
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "vaelix.exe"
    or InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "Ditto.exe"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, RemoteIP, RemotePort, RemoteUrl, InitiatingProcessFileName
| order by Timestamp asc
